On Windows, the names Chromium registers with Windows are ilo's own. As Chromium's, ilo shared
them with any Chromium on the machine: the AppUserModelID (base_app_id), which groups windows on
the taskbar and names the app a notification comes from; the toast activator CLSID, which a
Chromium's installer registers for its own notification helper; and the ProgIDs and Default
Programs name for links, HTML and PDF files. They're now app/branding/name's, as
app/platform/windows/package/ilo.iss registers them (IloHTML), and the CLSID is ilo's own. The
other GUIDs stay Chromium's: the elevation and tracing services and Active Setup belong to the
system-level installs Chromium's installer makes, which ilo's doesn't.

